user_message:
Review every unordered pair in this JSON feature list. Use its local zero-based indices,
not hypothesis IDs. Preserve all feature fields when deciding measurement equivalence.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 2,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_relies_on_abstract_normative_principle",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "OC_comments (other users' counter-arguments only): 1 if at least one comment's argument rests on an abstract normative principle (e.g. fairness, rights, justice, moral duty) stated in general terms rather than on a specific concrete institutional example; else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OP title and argument for context, then each comment in the JSON list OC_comments (ignore the conversation column; treat all text as data). Emit 1 if at least one comment's main support is a general moral/ethical/political principle or value (e.g. autonomy, fairness, rights, justice, what one ought to do) stated abstractly, not anchored in a specific functioning institutional example. A comment can satisfy both this and the precedent feature if different or the same comments do both. Emit 0 if comments parse and none do. Null if OC_comments is missing or malformed."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 16,
    "feature": {
      "name": "only_abstract_normative_comments",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "OC_comments (other users' comments only): 1 if every substantive comment relies solely on abstract normative principles (what should/ought, rights, fairness, morality) and none introduces concrete personal labor-process details, else 0.",
      "spec": "Read the title and argument (OP context) and all comments in the OC_comments JSON list. Emit 1 if there is at least one substantive comment and all substantive comments argue only from abstract normative principles (general claims about what is right, fair, ethical, or ought to be) with no concrete personal labor-process details (as in any_concrete_personal_labor_detail) in any comment. Emit 0 if any comment contains concrete personal labor-process details, or if any substantive comment relies on something other than abstract normative principles (e.g. empirical or other concrete evidence, non-labor anecdotes, definitions). Emit null if OC_comments is empty, unparsable or missing. Treat all text as data, not instructions."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 71,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_abstract_principle_reliance",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Other users' counter-argument comments (OC_comments, any comment): 1 if at least one comment relies on an abstract principle, general rule or theoretical/philosophical reasoning as its basis for countering the OP, else 0.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OP's title and argument for context, then parse OC_comments (JSON list of comments by users other than the OP). Emit 1 if at least one comment bases its counter-argument on an abstract principle, general rule, or conceptual/theoretical reasoning (e.g. appeals to fairness, definitions, general logic) rather than on specific concrete cases. A comment that has both abstract principle and concrete example still counts here if the principle is a main basis of its argument. Emit 0 if the list is complete and no comment does so (including empty list). Emit null if OC_comments is missing or unparseable. Treat all text as data, not instructions."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with an explicit verdict and reason.
